50 600.0 Td
(Step-by-Step Logic:) Tj
50 587.0 Td
(  1. Consider every ordered pair of points \(P_i, P_j\) as a candidate edge.) Tj
50 574.0 Td
(  2. For each candidate edge, check all remaining points P_k.) Tj
50 561.0 Td
(  3. Compute cross product of edge vector and vector to P_k.) Tj
50 548.0 Td
(  4. If all P_k have the same sign \(or are collinear\), edge is on hull.) Tj
50 535.0 Td
(  5. Collect all hull edges; extract unique hull vertices.) Tj
50 522.0 Td
(  6. Order hull vertices for boundary visualisation.) Tj
50 509.0 Td
() Tj
50 496.0 Td
() Tj
50 483.0 Td
(CORRECTNESS ARGUMENT) Tj
50 470.0 Td
(=====================) Tj
50 457.0 Td
(  Geometric Reasoning:) Tj
50 444.0 Td
(    An edge \(P_i, P_j\) lies on the convex hull boundary if and only if) Tj
50 431.0 Td
(    the ENTIRE point set lies on one side of the directed line P_i->P_j.) Tj
50 418.0 Td
() Tj
50 405.0 Td
(    WHY? The convex hull is the smallest convex polygon containing all points.) Tj
50 392.0 Td
(    Any edge of this polygon must have all points on one side \(the interior) Tj
50 379.0 Td
(    side\). If even ONE point were on the other side, the polygon would not) Tj
50 366.0 Td
(    be convex at that edge -- a contradiction.) Tj
50 353.0 Td
() Tj
50 340.0 Td
(    The cross product gives the signed area of the triangle P_i, P_j, P_k.) Tj
50 327.0 Td
(    Its sign indicates which side of the directed line P_k lies on.) Tj
50 314.0 Td
(    If ALL cross products have the same sign, ALL points are on ONE side.) Tj
50 301.0 Td
(    Therefore the edge is a valid convex hull edge.) Tj
50 288.0 Td
() Tj
50 275.0 Td
(    This is a purely geometric argument -- it does not rely on program output.) Tj
50 262.0 Td
() Tj
50 249.0 Td
() Tj
50 236.0 Td
(COMPLEXITY ANALYSIS) Tj
50 223.0 Td
(====================) Tj
50 210.0 Td
(  For n points:) Tj
50 197.0 Td
(    Outer loop:  n * \(n-1\) edge candidates) Tj
50 184.0 Td
(    Inner loop:  up to \(n-2\) point checks per edge) Tj
50 171.0 Td
() Tj
50 158.0 Td
(  Total edge checks = n * \(n-1\) * \(n-2\) in O\(n^3\)) Tj
50 145.0 Td
() Tj
50 132.0 Td
(  n   | Edge Checks | Growth factor) Tj
50 119.0 Td
(  ----+-------------+--------------) Tj
50 106.0 Td
(   5  |       60    |    --) Tj
50 93.0 Td
(  10  |      720    |   12x) Tj
